{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL0hvbGRpbmclMjBUaGVzZSUyME1vbWVudHMlMjAlMjgyMDIwJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Holding These Moments","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/esRKVPv1NtnmJLcskcMs2HSgtHR.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mBWGzVG7hbppUaiobPu34HqrOYK.jpg","description":"In early 2016, Dan Elswick embarked to document BANE’s final US tour. Starting as a love letter to his favorite band, it turned into much more. Beginning at a time when hardcore music strayed from its punk roots, BANE musically and lyrically challenged people. Five individuals set a course to live and play music by their own rules. After two decades attracting fans with their honesty as people and musicians, the pressure of home life and self-doubt became unavoidable. BANE made an all-or-nothing decision to end the band with a final album and tour. Holding These Moments examines the challenges of living and creating art on your own terms. It explores the artist’s struggle: questioning relevance and living a life of meaning amidst one’s art. Through extensive band, fan, and friend interviews, we see firsthand the impact of people living less ordinarily.\n\nReleased 13 Oct 2020 · US · Language: English · 110 min\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Documentary","Music","Hollywood"],"runtime":"110 min","cast":["Zach Jordan","Nicholas Branigan","Brendan Stu Maguire","Peter Chilton","Aaron Dalbec","Ben Chused","Nate Manning","James Siboni"],"director":["Dan Elswick"],"released":"2020-10-13T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"These words. These miles. These moments.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Dan Elswick","character":"Director"},{"name":"Zach Jordan","character":"Self"},{"name":"Nicholas Branigan","character":"Self"},{"name":"Brendan Stu Maguire","character":"Self"},{"name":"Peter Chilton","character":"Self"},{"name":"Aaron Dalbec","character":"Self"},{"name":"Ben Chused","character":"Self"},{"nam